{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"FIX PUSHED — Gerrit change 1640 'Fast-abort ACLI auth failure on stderr marker', awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.\n\nWHAT CHANGED (2 source files, 1 new test file, +279/-3):\n\n1. src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/acli_subprocess.py\n   - Added _AUTH_FAILURE_MARKERS + _is_auth_failure(stderr): detects credential rejection where ACLI actually reports it (stderr), matched case-insensitively. Kept deliberately TIGHT — credential-rejection wording only ('unauthorized', 'auth login', 'authentication failed', 'invalid credentials'), NOT authorization/permission wording ('forbidden', 'cannot be assigned'), so a data/permission fault is never reported to an operator as an expired credential.\n   - Added typed AcliAuthError(RuntimeError) carrying cmd + stderr, chaining the CalledProcessError per PEP 3134. Subclasses RuntimeError so existing 'except RuntimeError' sites in the acli path are unaffected.\n   - The retry loop now fast-aborts on the FIRST attempt via stderr marker OR the legacy 401 exit code (the 401 check is retained so a future ACLI that does propagate the status still fast-aborts).\n\n2. src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py\n   - _reconcile_exception_result classifies AcliAuthError as INVALID_INVOCATION (canonical exit 2) rather than OPERATIONAL_FAILURE (exit 1), with details['error_class']='auth_failed' and a message naming JIRA_API_TOKEN as the secret to rotate. Matched by TYPE NAME, not isinstance, to preserve that function's adapter-neutral posture (it must not import the Jira/ACLI adapter to classify a pass).\n\n3. tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_acli_auth_failure.py — 19 tests.\n\nREGRESSION COVERAGE VERIFIED, not change-detector: I ran the new tests against the pre-fix behaviour (markers emptied, so exit-code-only detection). Old code retried 3 times and raised a generic CalledProcessError — the fast-abort and typed-error tests genuinely fail against it.\n\nGATES: make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS (mypy, 504 source files); full tests/unit/rebar_reconciler suite 2401 passed. Both touched files remain under the 800-LOC module-size cap (acli_subprocess.py 526, __main__.py 750).\n\nAC STATUS:\n- AC 'detected from stderr not a 401 exit' — MET (test asserts the verbatim failed-run stderr with returncode=1 is recognised).\n- AC 'aborts on first attempt' — MET (test asserts exactly 1 spawn; was 3).\n- AC 'distinct typed error' — MET.\n- AC 'operator-facing message names the credential' — MET (INVALID_INVOCATION, exit 2, message names JIRA_API_TOKEN; asserts the generic 'reconcile_once raised' phrasing is absent).\n- AC 'non-auth failures keep retry behaviour' — MET (regression test: 3 attempts, backoff [2,4]).\n- AC 'Mode 1/Mode 2 relationship recorded' — MET (prior comment: independent).\n- AC 'misattributed faults filed as linked tickets' — MET, 4 filed and linked discovered_from: subzero-locustal-junebug (TLS cert verification), freeborn-dizzy-raven (rejected ref pushes), callous-wavy-kite (422 disabled-workflow re-dispatch), satisfied-emerald-grayling (swallowed 'command cancelled' noise).\n- AC 'lint/typecheck/tests pass' — MET.\n\nSTILL REQUIRES AN OPERATOR ACTION, NOT SHIPPABLE IN CODE: the JIRA_API_TOKEN secret is genuinely expired/revoked. This change makes that legible in one line instead of a generic red run, but the bridge will keep failing Mode 1 until the secret is ROTATED. Rotating it needs a new secret value and is outside what this ticket can deliver.\n\nNOTED, NOT FIXED (deliberate scope discipline): dispatch_one.py:790 has a best-effort 'except Exception' around link ops that would swallow an AcliAuthError raised mid-link-apply as non-fatal. That is not a regression (the old CalledProcessError was swallowed there too, and worse — counted as links_applied), and the observed failures all occur on the first search call, well before link ops. Flagged here rather than widened into this change."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786518238872309001,"uuid":"b16bbb9c-b73a-42d0-9a6a-5c97560fe5d3"}